{{ skills }}

These skills may be relevant to the current conversation — they are hints, not the full catalog. When one fits the user's request, activate it with `activate_skill` before you respond; don't wait until you need its tools. Activating costs nothing and is trivially reversible: if it turns out not to fit, just don't follow its instructions and carry on. When in doubt, activate — lean toward trying a skill, not toward skipping it. Don't ask the user whether to use a skill; just activate it when it seems relevant. The exception is a skill marked as needing a connection: activating it asks the user to connect that integration, so activate it only when their request depends on it, and say so in a short line first (e.g. "Let me bring in my health skill for that."). If none of these fit but the task seems to need a capability you don't have loaded, call `search_skills` with a short description of what you need.
